  "body": "## What changed\n\n`OpParams::stamp_with`, Wire Contour arm (`crates/app/src/operation/params.rs`): the side was written as `u8::from(side == Punch)`, so Die, Left and Right digested alike, and the run-out clearance was never written. An open run turned left <-> right, or given a new clearance, kept its stamp, so its old path (kerf on the side the user no longer states) read Ok and could post.\n\nThe side now writes its own discriminant, and an open run also writes its clearance:\n\n| Side | Bytes written |\n|---|---|\n| Die | `0` (as before) |\n| Punch | `1` (as before) |\n| Left | `2`, then the clearance |\n| Right | `3`, then the clearance |\n\n**Existing stamps:** die and punch stamps are byte-identical to before, so no closed cut goes Stale on upgrade, and a closed cut's clearance (which it never reads) still moves nothing. An open (Left/Right) run generated before this change reads Stale once after load and clears on regenerate. That is the one-time churn every stamp change causes. No golden or roundtrip fixture pins a wire stamp value: no committed `.ccam`/JSON fixture holds a `wire_contour`, and `golden_cl` pins CL output, not stamps.\n\nThe change is limited to the one stamp arm, plus a new test file. Open wire PRs #1163, #1181 and #1218 touch or move the same arm (they add `taper_deg` next to it and keep the old `== Punch` byte). Whichever merges second keeps both changes.\n\n## How tested\n\nNew suite `crates/app/tests/wire_stamp.rs`:\n- `an_open_runs_side_and_clearance_each_mark_its_path_stale`: a generated open cut-off is saved, its side is turned (and, separately, its clearance re-stated) in the file, and it is reopened with its old path and stamp. It reads Stale in both cases. Through the commands, the edit reads Stale and undo reads Ok.\n- `the_four_sides_stamp_apart_and_a_closed_cut_ignores_the_clearance`: all four sides give distinct `current_stamp`s. Die and punch ignore the clearance. Left and right read it.\n- `an_unrelated_edit_and_a_round_trip_leave_the_cuts_ok`: another operation's edit, a closed punch's clearance re-stated in its file, and a plain save/load all leave the cuts Ok.\n\nThe first two tests fail on `upstream/main` without the fix (checked by reverting `params.rs`), and all three pass with it.\n\nSuites run green: `wire_stamp`, `wire_contour`, `wire_burnout`, `wire_post`, `wire_readers`, `wire_verify`, `project_roundtrip`, `operations`, `golden_cl`. `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` and `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` both pass on the final head.\n\n**Why the file door:** `EditOperationParams` drops the stamp on every edit, so an edit always reads Stale and cannot prove the digest. The paths that keep a stamp are a project file and the stored stamp it reloads, so the pin goes through the file.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe GUI wire page, and a real EDM control.\n\nChangelog: An open wire run edited left <-> right, or given a new run-out clearance, now reads Stale instead of keeping its old path (#1370)\n\nEffort: high (not escalated)\n\nFork synced at v0.18.0 (process files at upstream PROCESS_VERSION 46); branch from upstream/main ebaceb1c.\n\nFixes #1370\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
